 - `session.py:65`: `Turn`.
 - `formatter.py`: `ChatFormatter.drop_messages`.
 
+**Proposed change (page segments): a page is its own exchange.**
+- The panel sends the page and the question as two parts (`runtime.PAGE_PREFIX`).
+  The page goes in as a user message with a reply the server writes
+  (`session.PAGE_ACK`), so templates that require alternating roles accept it.
+- Compaction drops, in order: pages a newer page replaced; middle exchanges,
+  oldest first; the current page. The anchor is now the first exchange that is
+  not a page.
+- A page at the very start of a conversation is cut so the KV is left as if the
+  question had come first. Dropping it naively left the page reply's closing
+  marker at position 0, and the model then replied with garbage (test 94).
+- A session compacting for its own new turn may also drop the latest exchange,
+  since the new turn becomes the latest. Other sessions still can't drop it.
+- The server keeps no page text. `status` names the page in context; when it no
+  longer matches, the panel re-reads the page with the next question.
+- **Trade-offs.** Re-reading costs prefill again. A follow-up with page text
+  unticked has no page. A re-read page sits after the earlier answers.
+
